    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point in **Kyle Tucker**, who secures our highest efficiency score at 66.85. Facing Landen Roupp, **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a favorable SP_xERA of 4.07 and a solid spot in the order, serving as our primary anchor in a lineup that is otherwise forced to navigate a difficult matchup against Corbin Burns. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** also projects as a strong play (59.34) despite the matchup against Burns; his score is significantly buoyed by a +14% dynamic platoon edge and a +5% wind-out factor in his stadium, providing the best path to value among our middle infield options today. \n\nOur bench management today is largely dictated by the \"Lineup Pending\" status of several players, including **Sam Antonacci** and **Andy Pages**. **Andy Pages** narrowly outperformed several alternatives with a score of 58.80, his inclusion driven by a clean neutral platoon matchup against Roupp and the benefit of hitting in the cleanup spot. The most difficult decision rested with **Drake Baldwin** and **Liam Hicks**; while both occupy the 50\u201352 score range, **Liam Hicks** earns the nod over lower-floor bench options due to a favorable +11% dynamic platoon split against an opposing righty. We are monitoring **Sam Antonacci** closely\u2014while his score (45.31) is lower than preferred, his elite 0.403 xwOBA keeps him in the starting nine as we prioritize his offensive ceiling over potentially stagnant bench depth.\n\nBeyond the pending lineup statuses, the primary risk for the Waves today is the gauntlet of Corbin Burns, whose 3.01 xERA is suppressing the projections for **Nasim Nunez** and **Brady House**. Both are skating on the edge of our \"marginal\" threshold. We remain cautious with **Dominic Smith** (41.51), who sits dangerously close to our floor; should the actual batting order shift him out of the seven-hole, we may look to re-evaluate our game cap usage to preserve flexibility for upcoming series against weaker rotations. All eyes remain on the statuses of **Luis Robert Jr.** and our inactive stars like **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Gunnar Henderson**, as we continue to manage our roster health heading into the middle of May.",
